2. DOUBLE-ENTRY ACCOUNTING
==========================

Implement a proper double-entry bookkeeping system.

Every journal entry must contain one or more journal lines.

Each journal line must contain:

* Account
* Debit
* Credit
* Description

Accounting rule:

TOTAL DEBIT = TOTAL CREDIT

Example:

Journal:

Dr Cash 100,000
Cr Capital 100,000

The system must reject:

Dr Cash 100,000
Cr Capital 90,000

Because:

Debit = 100,000
Credit = 90,000

The journal must not be posted.

Also reject a journal where:

Debit = 0
Credit = 0

A journal line must contain either:

Debit OR Credit

Never both.

Never allow negative Debit or Credit values.

==================================================
3. JOURNAL ENTRY STATUS SYSTEM
==============================

Implement the following statuses:

DRAFT
PENDING_APPROVAL
APPROVED
POSTED
REVERSED
CANCELLED

Workflow:

DRAFT
↓
PENDING APPROVAL
↓
APPROVED
↓
POSTED

Depending on user permissions, an authorized user may be able to post directly.

Only POSTED journals affect:

* General Ledger
* Account Balances
* Trial Balance
* Profit & Loss
* Balance Sheet

DRAFT journals must NOT affect financial reports.

PENDING_APPROVAL journals must NOT affect financial reports.

APPROVED journals must NOT affect financial reports until posted.

CANCELLED journals must NOT affect financial reports.

REVERSED journals must be handled through a proper reversal journal.

