23. IMPORTANT ACCOUNTING RULES
==============================

Never:

* Delete posted journals.
* Edit posted journals.
* Allow unbalanced journals.
* Allow inactive accounts to receive postings.
* Allow parent accounts to receive postings if manual posting is disabled.
* Create financial entries outside the central accounting engine.
* Update account balances manually.
* Use hardcoded account IDs.
* Allow duplicate journal numbers.
* Allow duplicate posting of the same source transaction.

Prepare the architecture for future idempotency protection.

For future automated transactions, the system should be able to identify:

Source Module
Source Transaction Type
Source Transaction ID

This will help prevent duplicate accounting entries.

